title: 'HRMP: widen the accepted origins and let paras make a few free requests'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    In Polkadot HRMP, in preparation for AHMv2:

    - Widen the accepted origins of `establish_system_channel` and `poke_channel_deposits`.
    - Expose `max_para_request_weight`, the weight of the heaviest request a parachain makes for
      itself.
    - Expose `ParaRequestCalls`, the calls a parachain makes for itself, each as its pallet
      index and its call index. It fits the `AllowedCalls` of the pallet `unpaid_transact`.

    Westend allows them in its pallet `unpaid_transact`, for a message that weighs no more than
    an HRMP request: a non-system parachain gets 10 HRMP requests per day executed without
    payment.
crates:
- name: polkadot-runtime-parachains
  bump: major
- name: pallet-hrmp-relay
  bump: patch
- name: westend-runtime
  bump: minor
